      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define what “memory disorder” means; it only discusses “memory impaired by injury or disease” and studies of memory retention/recall in patients.",
        "The definition’s claim that memory impairment involves “memory retention or recall” is only indirectly supported by the described “delayed recognition (DR) recall” and “memory retention,” without linking this description to the definition of the term “memory disorder.”",
        "The definition claims memory impairment “may be linked to injury or disease,” which is supported by the packet’s discussion of injury/disease-linked memory impairment, but the definition also contains additional claims (as a general term definition) that are not explicitly supported by the packet."
